2 CONT
2 CONT Born 	1344
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	11 June 1393 (aged 48-49)
2 CONT
2 CONT John of Bourbon-La Marche (John I/VII, Count of La Marche and of Vendôme), (1344 – 11 June 1393, Vendôme) was the second son of James I, Count of La Marche and Jeanne of Châtillon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [show]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 1 Life
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 2 Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 3 Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 4 References
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Life
2 CONT
2 CONT He was captured as a young man at the Battle of Poitiers, but ransomed.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his father and elder brother following the Battle of Brignais, John succeeded them as Count of La Marche.
2 CONT
2 CONT He took an active part in the Hundred Years' War, and became Governor of Limousin after helping reconquer it from the English. Later he joined Bertrand du Guesclin in his campaign of 1366 in Castile. In 1374, his brother-in-law Bo
2 CONC uchard VII, Count of Vendôme died, and John became Count of Vendôme and Castres in right of his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined the campaign of Charles VI 1382 in Flanders (which culminated in the Battle of Roosebeke) and fought in 1392 in Brittany.
2 CONT
2 CONT He rebuilt the castles of Vendôme and Lavardin.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 September 1364, he married Catherine of Vendôme, countess of Vendôme (d. 1412) and daughter of John VI, Count of Vendôme.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He had seven children by Catherine:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * James II, Count of La Marche and Castres (1370–1438)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Isabelle (b. 1373), a nun at Poissy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Louis, Count of Vendôme (1376–1446)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * John, Lord of Carency (1378–1457), married c. 1416 Catherine, daughter of Philip of Artois, Count of Eu, without issue, married in 1420 at Le Mans, his mistress Jeanne de Vendômois, with whom he had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anne (c. 1380 – September 1408, Paris), married in 1401 John of Berry, Count of Montpensier (d. 1401), married in Paris in 1402 Louis VII, Duke of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Marie (1386 – aft. September 11, 1463), Lady of Brehencourt, married Jean de Baynes, Lord of Croix
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Charlotte (1388 – 15 January 1422), married in 1411 at Nicosia King Janus of Cyprus
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Notes
2 CONT
