1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John VIII de Bourbon (1425 – 6 January 1478) was Count of Vendôme from 1446 until his death. A member of the House of Bourbon, he was the son and successor''' of Louis, Count of Vendôme.[1]''' As a courtier of K
2 CONC ing Charles VII of France, he fought the English in Normandy and Guyenne. He attached himself to King Louis XI, but was not in royal favor. He withdrew to the Château of Lavardin and completed its construction.
2 CONT In 1454, he married Isabelle de Beauvau''',[2] daughter of Louis de Beauvau, Marshal of Provence[3] and Marguerite de Chambley. '''They had''':
2 CONT *Jeanne (1460-1487), married in 1477 to Louis of Joyeuse
2 CONT *Catherine, married Gilbert de Chabannes
2 CONT *Jeanne, married at first John II, Duke of Bourbon and later John III, Count of Auvergne[4]
2 CONT *Renée, Abbess of Fontevraud
2 CONT *François, Count of Vendôme (1470–1495)[5]
2 CONT *Louis, Prince of La Roche-sur-Yon[2]
2 CONT *Catherine, married Engelbert, Count of Nevers[6]
2 CONT *Isabelle, Abbess of la Trinité de Caen
2 CONT '''Jean also had two illegitimate sons'''  :
2 CONT *Louis, Bishop of Avranches[7]
2 CONT *Jacques, Governor of Valois and the Vendomois (1455–1524) was the father of Catherine de Bourbon, paternal grandmother of Gabrielle d'Estrées, mistress of Henry IV of France. Also, Gabrielle is the third great aunt of Mathieu Ami
2 CONC ot.
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_VIII,_Count_of_Vend%C3%B4me
2 CONT '''John VIII'''
2 CONT '''Born	1425'''
2 CONT '''Died	6 January 1477 (aged 51–52)'''
2 CONT '''Lavardin'''
2 CONT '''Spouse	Isabelle de Beauvau'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Louis, Count of Vendôme
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Jeanne de Laval
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Jean II de Bourbon, Comte de Vendôme'''1 
2 CONT M, #113704, '''b. between 1425 and 1446, d. 6 January 1477'''
2 CONT Last Edited=2 Jun 2013
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.02%
2 CONT '''     Jean II de Bourbon, Comte de Vendôme was born between 1425 and 1446. He was the son''' of Louis de Bourbon, Comte de Vendôme and Jeanne de Laval.1 '''He was baptised before 1464. He married Isabel de Beauveau''', daughter 
2 CONC of Louis de Beauveau, Seigneur de Champigny and Margaret de Chambley, '''on 9 November 1454. He died on 6 January 1477'''.1
2 CONT '''     He gained the title of Comte de Vendôme'''.1
2 CONT '''Children of Jean II de Bourbon, Comte de Vendôme and Isabel de Beauveau'''
2 CONT 1. Louis de Bourbon, Prince de Roche-sur-Yon+1 d. 1520
2 CONT 2. Jeanne de Bourbon+2 b. 1465, d. 22 Jan 1511
2 CONT 3. François de Bourbon, Duc de Vendôme+1 b. 1470, d. 1495
2 CONT 4. Charlotte de Bourbon-Vendôme+3 b. 1474, d. 14 Dec 1520
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 68. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT 2.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 236. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT 3.[S3268] Hans Harmsen, "re: Chester Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 21 August 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Chester Family."
2 CONT https://thepeerage.com/p11371.htm#i113704
