2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Msr. Guy Ballan d'Ibelin (b.c. 1280) and Mme. Isabella, dau of Baldwin d'Ibelin:
2 CONT --
2 CONT    D1 : Descendant 1 (b.c. 1302)
2 CONT --
2 CONT    D2 : Descendant 2 (b.c. 1328)
2 CONT -- 
2 CONT    D3 : Descendant 3 (b.c. 1359)
2 CONT --
2 CONT    D4 : Descendant 4 (b.c. 1388)
2 CONT --
2 CONT    D5:   Descendant 5 : Msr. Henri Evelin (b.c. 1419)
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Família francesa que esteve na conquista da Terra Santa con Roberto, Duque da Normandia, e que recebeu em doação de Balduíno, Rei de Jerusalém, a cidade de Beirute, que continuou na posse dos descendentes. Passou esta família a Ch
2 CONC ipre, mas, devido á perda da ilha, voltou a França, fixando-se em Ruão. Daqui veio para Portugal Carlos Evelin, capitão de cavalos, que serviu D. Afonso VI contra Castela e se casou, neste Reino, onde deixou geração, sendo por últ
2 CONC imo residente de França. Timbre: o leão do escudo.
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT French family that was involved in the conquest of the Holy Land with Robert, Duke of Normandy, and that received the city of Beirut as a donation from Baldwin, King of Jerusalem, which continued in the possession of their descend
2 CONC ants. This family moved to Cyprus, but, due to the loss of the island, they returned to France, settling in Rouen. From here, Carlos Yvelin, captain of horses, who served D. Afonso VI against Castile and married in this Kingdom, c
2 CONC ame to Portugal, where he left a generation, and was finally a resident of France. Timbre: the lion on the shield.
