2 CONC ica capitaneorum, marchionum ac ducum Mantuae usque ad annum 1550 ; Annales Mediolanenses , in LA Muratori, Rer. Ital. Script. , XVI, Mediolani 1730, col. 715; B. Aliprandi, Aliprandina or Chronicle of Mantua , edited by O. Begani
2 CONC , in Rer. Ital. Script. , 2nd ed., XXIV, 13, p. 122; P. Azario, Liber gestorum in Lombardy , edited by F. Cognasso, ibid., XVI, 4, pp. 37, 92; A. Possevino iunior, Gonzaga. Calci operis addita genealogia totius familiae , Mantuae 
2 CONC 1617, p. 306; LC Volta, Chronological-critical compendium of the history of Mantua since its foundation in our times , II, Mantua 1827, pp. 17, 21, 30, 37, 49; G. Pirchan, Italien und Karl IV. in der Zeit seiner zweiten Romfahrt ,
2 CONC  in Quellen und Forschungen aus dem Gebiete der Geschichte , Prag 1930, II, pp. 11, 26, 248; F. Amadei, Universal Chronicle of the City of Mantua , edited by G. Amadei - E. Mariani - G. Praticò, I, Mantua 1954, pp. 529, 561, 565; 
2 CONC F. Cognasso, The unification of Lombardy under Milan , in History of Milan , V,The lordship of the Visconti (1310-1392) , Milan 1955, pp. 324, 400; Mantova. History , I, G. Coniglio, From its origins to 1440 , Mantua 1958, pp. 377
2 CONC , 379, 381, 407; M. Vaini, Gonzaga research (1189 - early 15th century) , Florence 1994, pp. 46 s., 49 s .; P. Litta, The famous Italian families , sv Gonzaga , tav. II
