2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Paris, the son of King Charles V and Jeanne de Bourbon. At the age of eleven, he was crowned King of France in 1380 in the cathedral at Reims. He married Isabeau of Bavaria in 1385. Until he took complete charge as 
2 CONC king in 1388, France was ruled primarily by his uncle, Philip the Bold, Duke of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles VI was known both as Charles the Well-loved and later as Charles the Mad, since, beginning in his mid-twenties, he experienced bouts of psychosis. These fits of madness would recur for the rest of his life. Based on his sy
2 CONC mptoms, he probably suffered from schizophrenia.
2 CONT
