1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John, Dauphin of France and Duke of Touraine (31 August 1398 – 5 April 1417) was Dauphin of Viennois and Duke of Touraine. He inherited the Dauphin of Viennois in 1415, following the death of his older brother''
2 CONC ', Louis. '''He died 5 April 1417, and was succeeded by his brother''' Charles.
2 CONT Early life
2 CONT '''John was born in 1398,[1] the fourth son''' of Charles VI of France and Isabeau of Bavaria. '''At the age of four (in Paris on 5 May 1403) and again at the age of seven (in Compiègne on 29 June 1406), he was betrothed to Jacque
2 CONC line, heiress of the County of Hainaut, Holland, Zealand, and Frisia.[2] After his betrothal to Jacqueline, he was brought up alongside her at the castle of Le Quesnoy in Hainaut, at the court of his future mother-in-law''', Marga
2 CONC ret of Burgundy.[2] '''This arrangement was made between his father and his future father-in-law to ensure his safety away from the tumultuous court in Paris, as well as to acquaint him with the lands which he would rule as husban
2 CONC d of Jacqueline after her father's death.[3] As he was the king's fourth son, he was only expected to succeed to his wife's lands, and was not expected to become king.'''[3]
2 CONT '''On 22 April 1411 the Pope gave his dispensation for the union and on 6 August 1415, when John was sixteen, he and Jacqueline married in The Hague.'''[4]
2 CONT Dauphin
2 CONT '''Four months after his marriage, John's elder brother''' Louis, Dauphin of France, '''died on 18 December 1415, and John became the next Dauphin of France.'''
2 CONT Death
2 CONT '''John died on 5 April 1417 at the age of eighteen.[5] The cause of his death is disputed. According to some, he died from the consequences of an abscess in the head, while other sources suggest he had been poisoned.[6] He was bu
2 CONC ried in Compiègne's Saint-Corneille abbey. His younger brother''' Charles '''became dauphin and eventually king.'''[5]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John,_Duke_of_Touraine
2 CONT ________
2 CONT '''Jean, Duke de Torraine, Berry'''1,2
2 CONT Last Edited	4 Sep 2011
2 CONT M, #47747, '''b. 31 August 1398, d. 5 April 1417'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Charles VI 'the Mad', King of France1 b. 3 Dec 1368, d. 21 Oct 1422
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Isabeau of Bavaria1 b. 1371, d. 24 Sep 1435
2 CONT '''     Jean, Duke de Torraine, Berry was born on 31 August 1398 at Paris, France.1 He and Jacqueline of Holland obtained a marriage license on 22 April 1411; Date of Dispensation for being related in the 3rd and 4th degrees.2 Jea
2 CONC n, Duke de Torraine, Berry married Jacqueline of Holland''', daughter of Wilhelm VI, Count of Holland, Hennegau, Seeland, & Straubing, Lord of Arkel and Margarethe de Burgundy, '''on 6 August 1415 at Den Haag, Netherlands.1,3 Jean
2 CONC , Duke de Torraine, Berry died on 5 April 1417 at Compiegne, France, at age 18; Poisoned; buried at Abbey of St. Corneille.'''1,3,2
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Jacqueline of Holland''' b. 16 Jul 1401, d. 9 Oct 1436
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. II, Tafel 23.
2 CONT 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 550-551.
2 CONT 3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 432.
2 CONT From: https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1589.htm#i47747
