2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Orléans, Count of Angoulême (French: Charles d'Orléans, Comte d'Angoulême) (1459 – 1 January 1496) was a member of the French Orléans family descended from Louis I de Valois, Duke of Orléans, and a minor French prince. 
2 CONC He was Count of Angoulême from 1467-1496. He married three times, the third to Louise of Savoy, daughter of Philip the Landless and Margaret of Bourbon, in 1490. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite d'Angoulême (11 April 1492 – 21 December 1549)
2 CONT
2 CONT François d'Angoulême (12 September 1494 – 31 March 1547), who became King of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, Count of Angoulême
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Charles, Count of Angouleme)
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Orléans, Count of Angoulême (French: Charles d'Orléans, Comte d'Angoulême) (1459 – 1 January 1496) was a member of the French Orléans family descended from Louis I de Valois, Duke of Orléans, and a minor French prince. 
2 CONC He was the son of John, Count of Angoulême and Marguerite de Rohan, and was Count of Angoulême from 1467-1496. He married Louise of Savoy, daughter of Philip the Landless and Margaret of Bourbon, on 16 February 1488. They had two 
2 CONC children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite d'Angoulême (11 April 1492 – 21 December 1549)
2 CONT
2 CONT François d'Angoulême (12 September 1494 – 31 March 1547), who became King of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles also had two illegitimate daughters by his mistress Antoinette de Polignac, Dame de Combronde, who was his wife's lady-in-waiting:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne of Angouleme (c.1490- after 1531/1538), married firstly Jean Aubin, Seigneur de Malicorne, and secondly, Jean IV de Longwy, Baron of Pagny, by whom she had three daughters. The youngest, Jacqueline de Longwy (died 28 August
2 CONC  1561), in her own turn married Louis III de Bourbon, Duke of Montpensier.
2 CONT
2 CONT Madeleine d'Angouleme, Abbess of Fontevrault (died 26 October 1543)
2 CONT
2 CONT He also had an illegitimate daughter by mistress Jeanne Le Conte:
2 CONT
2 CONT Souveraine d'Angouleme (died 23 February 1551), married Michel III de Gaillard, Seigneur de Chilly.
2 CONT --------------------
