1 NOTE Maximilian I (1459-1519), German emperor, was the son of Frederick III, and was born at Neustadt, near Vienna. His fame is principally due to his efforts to reform the imperial and Austrian administrations. He was an accomplished 
2 CONC knight, and was very popular with the citizen classes. See Seton-Watson�s Maximilian I (1901), and Lodge�s Close of the Middle Ages. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
