2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p10749.htm#i107487 ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret de Baux, Countess of Saint-Pol, of Brienne, and of Conversano, sometimes known as Margherita del Balzo (1394- 15 November 1469), was a member of the noble del Balzo (de Baux) family of the Kingdom of Naples, which had its
2 CONC  origins in Provence dating back to the 11th Century. Her husband was Peter of Luxembourg, Count of Saint-Pol, of Brienne, and of Conversano (1390- 31 August 1433). Margaret's descendants include English Queen Consort Elizabeth Wo
2 CONC odville, King Henry IV of France, Mary, Queen of Scots, and all English monarchs after 1509.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alternative Spellings of Maiden Name:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * de Balzo
2 CONT * de Baux
2 CONT * del Balso _________________________
