1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''PLEASE READ THIS COMMENT REGARDING HIS BIRTH DATE;
2 CONT
2 CONT "Henry was born in the tower above the gatehouse of Monmouth Castle and for that reason called Henry of Monmouth, son of Henry of Bolingbroke, later Henry IV, and sixteen-year-old Mary de Bohun. Two dates are suggested: 9 August o
2 CONC r 16 September, in either 1386 or 1387."'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================================================================
2 CONT Henry became a Knight of the Garter in 1399.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry V 
2 CONT
2 CONT King of England; Prince Regent of France; Lord of Ireland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reign 21 March 1413 – 31 August 1422 
2 CONT
2 CONT Coronation 1413 
2 CONT
2 CONT Predecessor Henry IV 
2 CONT
2 CONT Successor Henry VI 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Catherine of Valois 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry VI 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Henry IV 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother Mary de Bohun 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 16 September 1387(1387-09-16)
2 CONT
2 CONT Monmouth, Wales 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 31 August 1422 (aged 34)
2 CONT
2 CONT Bois de Vincennes, France 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Westminster Abbey, London 
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT "Henry V (16 September 1386 – 31 August 1422) was King of England from 1413 until his death at the age of 35 in 1422. He was the second English monarch who came from the House of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT After military experience fighting various lords who rebelled against his father, Henry IV, Henry came into political conflict with the increasingly ill king. After his father's death, Henry rapidly assumed control of the country 
2 CONC and embarked on war with France. From an unassuming start, his military successes in the Hundred Years' War, culminating with his famous victory at the Battle of Agincourt, saw him come close to conquering France. After months of 
2 CONC negotiation with Charles VI of France, the Treaty of Troyes recognised Henry V as regent and heir-apparent to the French throne, and he was subsequently married to Charles's daughter, Catherine of Valois. Following Henry V's sudde
2 CONC n and unexpected death in France, he was succeeded by his infant son, who reigned as Henry VI.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry features in three plays by William Shakespeare. He is shown as a young scapegrace who redeems himself in battle in the two Henry IV plays and as a decisive leader in Henry V."
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================================================================
