1 OCCU Count of Flanders, Count of Nevers, and Count of Rethel, Ct Louis II "de Mâle"  of Flanders (1346-48), Comte de Nevers et Comte de Rethel (1346-84), Comte de Bourgogne et Comte d'Artois, Seigneur de Salins (1382-84), Graaf van Vla
2 CONC anderen
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.geni.com/people/Louis-II-van-Vlaanderen-Comte-de-Flandres-Flanders/6000000185363088822 '''LOUIS de Flandre'''], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Louis-II-Dampierre-comte-de-Nevers-de-Flandre-et-de-R
2 CONC ethel/6000000001500850848?through=6000000185363088822 LOUIS I] Count of Flanders & his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Marguerite-de-Flandre-Princesse-de-France-comtesse-de-Bourgogne-de-Nevers/6000000001096256553?through=6000000
2 CONC 185363088822 Marguerite de France] Ctss d'Artois (Maldeghem/Mâle, near Bruges 25 Nov 1330-Saint-Omer 30 Jan 1383, bur Lille Saint-Pierre).
2 CONT The Iohannis de Thilrode Chronicon names "Ludovicus…filius fuit Ludovicus dictus de Male"[810].  He succeeded his father in 1346 as LOUIS II “de Male” Count of Flanders, Comte de Nevers et de Rethel, Comte Palatin de Bourgogne, Co
2 CONC mte d'Artois.  After his brother-in-law Wenzel I Comte de Luxembourg, Duke of Brabant, initiated negotiations with his brother concerning the latter's eventual inheritance of the childless Wenzel's properties, Count Louis occupied
2 CONC  Mechelen and Duke Wenzel was forced to flee to Limburg.  The dispute was settled by the peace of Ath under which Mechelen and Antwerp were transferred to Flanders, and Count Louis was granted the right to bear the title Duke of B
2 CONC rabant[811].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed (Papal dispensation Avignon 14 Mar 1335) to his first cousin, [https://www.geni.com/people/Yolande-de-Dampierre-Dame-de-Cassel/6000000006409280949 YOLANDE de Flandre, dame de Cassel], daughter of ROBERT de Flandre, Comte
2 CONC  de Marle, Seigneur de Cassel & his wife Jeanne de Bretagne, dame de Nogent-le-Rotrou (château d'Alluyes, Eure-et-Loir 2 Feb or 15 Sep 1326 or 1331-château de Nieppe dit de La Motte-au-Bois, Hazebrouck, Nord 12 Dec 1395, bur Bar-l
2 CONC e-Duc, église collégiale Saint-Maxe). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed (before 1347, renewed 13 Mar 1347, terminated before 6 Jun 1347) to [https://www.geni.com/people/Isabella-Countess-of-Bedford/6000000003177905048 ISABELLA of England], daughter of EDWARD III King of England & his wife Ph
2 CONC ilippa de Hainaut (Woodstock Palace, Oxfordshire 16 Feb or [Mar] or 16 Jun [1332 or 1334]-[15 Mar/4 May] 1379 or [17 Jun/5 Oct] 1382, bur Greyfriars Church, Newgate, London).  A charter dated 13 Mar 1346 (O.S.) records the renewal
2 CONC  of the contract for the marriage between “Loys contes de Flandres, de Nevers et de Rechest” and “Edward...Roi d´Engleterre...Ysabel ainsnee fille”[812]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Saint-Quentin 6 Jun 1347) [https://www.geni.com/people/Margaretha-de-M%C3%A2le-Flanders-Nevers/6000000001504983220?through=6000000185363088822 MARGUERITE de Brabant], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/John-III-Duke-of-Br
2 CONC abant/5566580638230026755?through=6000000000498433774 JEAN III Duke of Brabant] & his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Marie-d-Evreux/6000000000498433774?through=6000000001504983220 Marie d'Evreux] (9 Feb 1323-1368, bur Lille Sai
2 CONC nt-Pierre).  The Oude Kronik van Brabant names "Johannam, Margaretam comitissam Flandrie, et Mariam coniugem Reynaldi Grossi ducis Ghelrie secundi" as the three daughters of "Johannes tertius" and his wife "Mariam filiam Ludowici 
2 CONC comitis Eboracensis"[813]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-III-Countess-of-Flanders/6000000004532537004?through=6000000001504983220 MARGUERITE de Flandre] (Mâle near Bruges 1350, chr 13 Apr 1350-Arras 16 Mar 1405, bur Lille, église Saint-P
2 CONC ierre).  The marriage contract between “Philippes Duc de Bourgongne” and “Marguerite de Flandres” is dated 21 Mar 1356 (O.S.)[814].  The Iohannis de Thilrode Chronicon records the marriage of "filiam comitis nostri Ludovici de Mal
2 CONC e Margaretam" and "Philippus filius regis Francie"[815].  A charter dated 20 Jul 1364 records negotiations for the marriage between “nostre...cousin le conte de Flandres...Margarete duchesse de Burgoigne file au dit conte” and “no
2 CONC stre...filz Esmon de Langele”[816].  The contract for the marriage between “Edward...roi Engleterre...messieur Esmon counte de Cantebrigg filz au dit roi” and “Loys counte de Flandres, duc de Brabant, counte de Nyvers et de Reches
2 CONC t et sire de Malynes...dame Margarete duchesse de Burgoigne sa fille”[817].  The Chronicon Angliæ records the betrothal of “Edmundus de Langley filius regis Edwardi” and “filiam et heredem...comitis Flandriæ”, adding that “rex Fra
2 CONC nciæ Karolus” blocked the marriage, dated to 1364 from the context[818].  She succeeded her father in 1383 as MARGUERITE III Ctss of Flanders, Ctss d'Artois, Ctss de Nevers and Rethel, Ctss Palatine of Burgundy.  Dss of Brabant an
2 CONC d Limburg, Markgravine of Antwerp, Dame de Malines 1404.  m firstly (Papal dispensation 31 Jan 1356, contract Paris 21 Mar 1357, Arras, église Saint-Vaast 14 May 1357, not consummated) [https://www.geni.com/people/Philippe-de-Rouv
2 CONC res-duc-de-Bourgogne/6000000006101415412?through=6000000004532537004  PHILIPPE I "de Rouvres" Duke of Burgundy], son of PHILIPPE "Monsieur" de Bourgogne [Capet], Comte d'Artois, Comte Palatin de Bourgogne, Comte d'Auvergne et de B
2 CONC oulogne & Jeanne I Ctss d'Auvergne et de Boulogne (château de Rouvres, Côte d'Or end Aug 1346-château de Rouvres 21 Nov 1361, bur Abbaye de Cîteaux).  Betrothed (19 Oct 1364) to [https://www.geni.com/people/Edmund-of-Langley-1st-D
2 CONC uke-of-York/6000000016643963931 EDMUND of Langley], son of EDWARD III King of England & his wife Philippa de Hainaut (Abbot’s Langley, Hertfordshire 5 Jun 1341-King’s Langley, Hertfordshire 1 Aug 1402, bur King’s Langley, Church o
2 CONC f the Dominican Friars).  This betrothal was arranged under the Treaty of Dover 19 Oct 1364, but the French persuaded Pope Urban V to refuse a dispensation on grounds of consanguinity[819].  m secondly (by proxy 12 Apr 1369, in pe
2 CONC rson Gent 19 Jun 1369) [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-II-the-Bold-Duke-of-Burgundy/6000000004526559011?through=6000000004532537004 PHILIPPE II "le Hardi" Duke of Burgundy], son of JEAN II "le Bon" King of France & his first w
2 CONC ife Bonne de Luxembourg (Pontoise 15 Jan 1342-Hall 27 Apr 1404, bur Dijon). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II had eleven illegitimate children by various mistresses (the order of their births is uncertain):
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >2. [https://www.geni.com/people/Louis/6000000205440539873 LOUIS "le Haeze"] (-killed in battle Nicopolis 28 Sep 1396). Espinoy records his parentage, noting that his father granted him “tous les biens de Messire Geeraert de Moor 
2 CONC chevalier”, from whom they had been confiscated for murdering “Messire Jean Tant chevalier”, by charter dated 1 Apr 1370 (no source citations)[820]. m --- de Landas, daughter of ---. The primary source which confirms her marriage 
2 CONC has not been identified. Louis [& his wife] had two children:
2 CONT >3. [https://www.geni.com/people/LOUIS/6000000205440789821 LOUIS "Friese"] (-killed in battle Nicopolis 28 Sep 1396). His mother is referred to in the following source: Vredius quotes a manuscript which records “messire Loys de Fr
2 CONC ise fils bastard de...Loys de Male conte de Flandre, lequel il eut d’une fille de Monsieur de Borre”[822].
2 CONT >4. [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean/6000000205440702826 JEAN "Sans Terre"] (-killed in battle Nicopolis 28 Sep 1396). Espinoy names “Jean de Flandres...le cinquiesme fils bastard du... [Comte Louys dit de Maele]...surnommé sans 
2 CONC terre”, to whom his father granted “le chastel et maison de Drincam”, which has been confiscated from “Jean de Scheuruelde...proche heritier de Jacques de Drincham dernier possesseur”, confirmed by charter dated 21 Nov 1383 (no so
2 CONC urce citation)[823].
2 CONT >5. [https://www.geni.com/people/Pierre/6000000205440587914 PIERRE] (-[3 Mar 1376]). A list of knights in Flanders dated [1384-86] names “mer Pieter de Bastaerd”[824]. Buylaert records that an epitaph at Gent Dominican church reco
2 CONC rds the burial of “Pieter van Vlaanderen bastaard van Lodewijk van Male” who died 3 Mar 1376 (O.S.?)[825]. It is unclear whether these two entries relate to the same person, but if so the epitaph must be misdated.
2 CONT >6. [https://www.geni.com/people/Rennikin/6000000205439959982 RENNEKIN] . 1394.
2 CONT >7. [https://www.geni.com/people/Gennikin/6000000205440913821 GENNEKIN] . 1394.
2 CONT >8. [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-van-Vlaanderen-heer-van-Elverdinghe/6000000002187845469 ROBERT] [Roeland] (-21 Jan 1434, bur Ghidts). Espinoy names “Robert de Flandres...le quatriesme fils bastard du... Comte Louys dit de 
2 CONC Maele...surnommé le Frison”, to whom his father granted “les terres et seigneuries d’Eluerdinge et Vlamertinge” (no source citation), adding that he was also “Vicomte d’Ypres”[826]. Seigneur d'Everdinghe et de Vlamertinghe. The te
2 CONC stament of “her Victor van Vlaendren”, dated 1430, named executors “m’her Robert van Vlaendren heere van Elverdinghe, Vlamertinghe, Burggrave van Ypre en Karle van Vlaendren beede sijn broeders”[827]. An epitaph at Ghijdts records
