1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kinloss Abbey is a Cistercian abbey at Kinloss in the county of Moray, Scotland. The abbey was founded in 1150 by King David  I  
2 CONT
2 CONT The County of Moray or Morayshire, called Elginshire until 1919,
2 CONT
2 CONT == JOHN GORDON Master of Huntly == 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on John Gordon, Lord Gordon:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10832.htm#i108314
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gordon, Lord Gordon [1]
2 CONT *M, #108314, 
2 CONT *d. 1517
2 CONT *Last Edited=25 Apr 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.78%
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gordon, Lord Gordon married Margaret Stewart, daughter of James IV Stewart, King of Scotland and Margaret Drummond, in November 1512.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1517.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Alexander Gordon, 3rd Earl of Huntly and Lady Jean Stewart.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was styled as Lord Gordon in 1501.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Gordon, Lord Gordon and Margaret Stewart
2 CONT *1. Alexander Gordon [2]
2 CONT *2. James Gordon [3]
2 CONT *3. George Gordon, 4th Earl of Huntly+[2] b. 1513, d. 22 Oct 1562
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 240. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
