1 NAME William /Hay/
2 GIVN William
2 SURN Hay
2 _MARNM Hay
1 NAME William Hay, 4th Earl of Erroll
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 SEP 1513
2 PLAC Flodden Field, Northumberland, England
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://thepeerage.com/p1745.htm#i17445
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Hay,_4th_Earl_of_Erroll '''William Hay, 4th Earl of Erroll''']
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hay, 4th Earl of Erroll (1470 – 9 September 1513), styled as Lord Hay until 1507, was a Scottish peer and soldier. He was killed at the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Flodden Battle of Flodden].
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography<br/>
2 CONT William Hay was the son of William Hay, 3rd Earl of Erroll. He had double royal lineage: his grandfather, William Hay, 1st Earl of Erroll was a great-great grandson of King Robert II of Scotland; and his maternal grandfather was J
2 CONC ames I of Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_High_Constable_of_Scotland Lord High Constable of Scotland], a hereditary title that was, after the king, the supreme officer of the Scottish army. He was killed on 9 September 
2 CONC 1513 in the Battle of Flodden, near Branxton, Northumberland. He died alongside his younger brother Thomas, King James IV of Scotland and more than a dozen dukes and earls in a decisive English victory.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue<br/>
2 CONT He married Christian Lyon, daughter of John Lyon, 3rd Lord Glamis, and had two children:<br/>
2 CONT 1. William Hay, 5th Earl of Erroll (c. 1495, Errol, Perthshire, Scotland – 28 July 1522 in Edinburgh)<br/>
2 CONT 2. Lady Isabel Hay<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT He married secondly Margaret Kinloch of Cruvie, widow of Sir James Sandilands, 5th feudal baron of Calder.
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Flodden
2 CONT * http://www.cyberancestors.com/cummins/ps112/ps112_322.htm
2 CONT * http://histfam.familysearch.org/getperson.php?personID=I16382&tree=Nixon
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Hay,_4th_Earl_of_Erroll
