1 NOTE KING OF PORTUGAL 1578-1580
1 NOTE Henry (of Portugal) (1512-80), king of Portugal (1578-80), son of King 
2 CONT Emanuel of Portugal. Henry was educated for the priesthood and at about 
2 CONT age 27 was consecrated bishop of Evora and appointed grand inquisitor of 
2 CONT Portugal. Under his direction the Inquisition became a powerful force in 
2 CONT the country, and Henry was made a cardinal in 1545. He acted as regent for 
2 CONT his nephew, King Sebastian (1554-78), during the minority of the young 
2 CONT king. In 1578 Henry succeeded to the throne when Sebastian was killed at 
2 CONT the Battle of the Three Kings in Morocco. Henry left no heir, and the Avis 
2 CONT dynasty ended with him. Philip II of Spain succeeded him as king of 
2 CONT Portugal.
