2 CONT '''m''' (Papal dispensation 17 Jul 1247) ISABELLE Rivet, daughter of AIMERY Rivet & his wife Eschiva de Saint-Omer.  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Ysabeau, la fille de Heimeri de Rivet et de Eschive de Thabarie" as the wife of Jea
2 CONC n son of "Bauduin, fis Jehan de Ybelin, seignor de Barut…seneschau dou Chipre"[645].  The dispensation issued by Pope Innocent IV for the marriage of "Jean Ibelin filius Balduini fratris domini Beritensis" and "Isabeau nata Aymeri
2 CONC ci de Rivet" is dated 17 Jul 1247[646].  This marriage was arranged as part of the reconciliation with the families who had supported Emperor Friedrich II King of Germany in the Cypriot civil war 1229/32[647].
