1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Margaret of Villehardouin was then in Sicily, seeking to advance her claim to the Principality of Achaea. She gave her daughter Isabelle de Sabran to Ferdinand in marriage and resigned Mategrifon and her claim on A
2 CONC chaea to the couple, who were married in Messina. Margaret died in March 1315 in her castle of Akova in the Morea, and her daughter on May 7, 1315 in Catania, shortly after bearing a son, James III of Majorca.
