2 CONT *'''     Edward Plantagenet, Prince of Wales was born on 13 October 1453 at Palace of Westminster, Westminster, London, England.2 He was the son''' of Henry VI Plantagenet, King of England and Margaret d'Anjou.1 '''He married Lady
2 CONC  Anne Beauchamp Neville''', daughter of Richard Neville, 16th Earl of Warwick and Lady Anne Beauchamp, '''on 13 December 1470 at Château d'Amboise, Amboise, Bourgogne, France.2 He died on 4 May 1471 at age 17 at Tewkesbury, Glouce
2 CONC stershire, England, killed in action, without issue.2
2 CONT *'''     He was created 1st Duke of Cornwall [England] on 13 October 1453.2 He was created 1st Earl of Chester [England] on 15 March 1454.2 He was created Prince of Wales [England] on 9 June 1454.2 He was invested as a Knight, Ord
2 CONC er of the Garter (K.G.).2 He fought in the Battle of Tewkesbury on 4 May 1471 at Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire, England.
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct
2 CONC  or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 174. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 132. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
