2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (1265 – May 1276). He was poisoned, possibly by orders of his stepmother. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip IV (1268 – November 29, 1314), successor as king. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert (1269 - 1271). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles (March 12, 1270 – December 16, 1325), Count of Valois. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stillborn son (1271). 
2 CONT
2 CONT After Isabella's death, he married on 21 August 1274, Marie de Brabant, daughter of Henry III of Brabant and Adelaide of Burgundy. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (May 1276 – May 19, 1319), Count of Évreux. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca (1278 – March 19, 1305, Vienna), married Rudolf III of Austria on May 25, 1300. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite (1282 – February 14, 1317), married Edward I of England 
