1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mesih Pasha''' or Misac Pasha[1] (died November 1501) was an Ottoman statesman of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantine_Greeks Byzantine Greek] origin, being a nephew of the last Roman emperor, [https://www.g
2 CONC eni.com/people/Constantine-XI-Palaiologos-last-byzantine-emperor/6000000009965401953 '''Constantine XI Palaiologos''']. He served as [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapudan_Pasha Kapudan Pasha] of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki
2 CONC /Ottoman_Navy Ottoman Navy] and was [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Ottoman_grand_viziers Grand Vizier] of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman_Empire Ottoman Empire] in 1501. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesih_Pasha En], [https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesih_Pa%C5%9Fa Tr]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesih_Pasha#Life Life]===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesih_Pasha#Origin_and_early_life '''Origin and early life''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Mesih was related to the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaiologos Palaiologoi], the last ruling dynasty of the Byzantine Empire. According to the 16th-century Ecthesis Chronica, he was the son of a certain [https://www.geni.com/
2 CONC people/Gidos-Palaiologos/6000000205092417878 '''Gidos Palaiologos'''], identified by the contemporary Historia Turchesca (attributed to Donado da Lezze or Giovanni Maria Angiolello) as a brother of a Byzantine emperor.[2] This emp
2 CONC eror is commonly held to have been [https://www.geni.com/people/Constantine-XI-Palaiologos-last-byzantine-emperor/6000000009965401953 '''Constantine XI Palaiologos'''], the last Byzantine emperor, who was killed during the Fall of
2 CONC  Constantinople to the Ottoman Sultan [https://www.geni.com/people/Mehmed-II-bin-Murad-Han-The-Conqueror-Ottoman-Sultan/385223927880013853 '''Mehmed II'''] in 1453.[3] If true, since [https://www.geni.com/people/Constantine-XI-Pal
2 CONC aiologos-last-byzantine-emperor/6000000009965401953 '''Constantine XI'''] died childless, and had the Ottomans failed to conquer Constantinople, Mesih or his brother [https://www.geni.com/people/Hass-Murad-Pasha/600000020509264282
2 CONC 6 '''Hass Murad Pasha'''] might have succeeded him. Instead, Mesih rose to become one of the most powerful men in the state that destroyed the Byzantine Empire.[4] The Byzanto-Italian chronicler [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theo
2 CONC dore_Spandounes Theodore Spandounes], who claimed that Mesih was the brother of his own paternal grandmother, wrote that Mesih was ten years old at the time of Constantinople's fall. He and two of his brothers, one of whom was  [h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/people/Hass-Murad-Pasha/6000000205092642826 '''Hass Murad'''], were captured, converted to Islam, and raised as pages under the auspices of Sultan [https://www.geni.com/people/Mehmed-II-bin-Murad-Han-The-Conque
2 CONC ror-Ottoman-Sultan/385223927880013853 '''Mehmed II'''], as part of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devshirme devşirme] system.[2][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesih_Pasha#Career_under_Mehmed_II '''Career under Mehmed II''']
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesih_Pasha#Rise_under_Bayezid_II '''Rise under Bayezid II''']
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesih_Pasha#Disgrace_and_restoration_to_favour '''Disgrace and restoration to favour''']
