1 NOTE {geni:about_me} PRINCESS BEATRICE of PORTUGAL COUNTESS OF ARUNDEL & HUNTINGDOM
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.sueandgordon.co.uk/page51.htm#b10500
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Beatrice (also Beatrix, Beatriz) 1382 – November 1439, was a natural daughter of John I King of of Portugal and Inês Pires born before the marriage of her father with Philippa of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a sister of Afonso Duke of Braganza, half-sister of King Edward of Portugal, Infante Peter Duke of Coimbra, Henry the Navigator, Isabella of Portugal Duchess of Burgundy, John Constable of Portugal, and Ferdinand the Saint
2 CONC  Prince. Queen Philippa was in charge of the education of both of her husband's children out of wedlock.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice was born 1382, possibly in Veiros, Alentejo, Portugal. Some say that her mother Inês Pires was "the daughter of a Jewish cobbler." But others say she came from an old Portuguese noble line. In April 1405 her wedding with 
2 CONC Thomas Fitzalan 12th Earl of Arundel by proxy was celebrated in Lisbon and, in the same year, she traveled to England, accompanied by her brother Afonso and many of the king's vassals and her ladies-in-waiting where the marriage c
2 CONC eremony took place on 26 November 1405 in London, with King Henry IV in attendance.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas died on 13 October 1415. Beatrice then married John Holland Earl of Huntingdon (verified in her Coat of Arms) who was the nephew of her stepmother Queen Philippa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is sometimes confused with another Portuguese lady, Beatrice Pinto, wife of Gilbert Talbot and Thomas Fittiplace. It is unknown if Beatrice had children from any of her marriages. Beatrice died in Bordeaux, France in November 
2 CONC 1439. After her death her husband married Lady Anne Montagu. 
