2 NOTE This image provides the Heraldic Evidence needed to move from a "theoretical" bastardy mark to the Specific Jurisdictional Arms of the Seigneury of Praet.
3 CONT
3 CONT In heraldry, when a noble bastard was granted a specific, ancient lordship (like Praet), they often abandoned the "Baton" or "Bendlet" of illegitimacy in favor of Arms of Patronage. This image confirms that Louis used a Canton of 
3 CONC Flanders (the lion) over the Vert (green) field of the Moerkerke/Praet lineage.
