1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fran%C3%A7ois_II_de_La_Tr%C3%A9moille
2 CONT
2 CONT François de La Trémoille (1505-1541) was a French nobleman of the La Tremoille family. He was the son of Charles I de la Trémoille (killed in 1515 at the battle of Marignan) and of Louise de Coëtivy, and the grandson of Louis II d
2 CONC e la Trémoille and of Gabrielle de Bourbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Titles He held the title of 36th vicomte of Thouars (1525-1541). His other titles were prince de Talmont and comte of Taillebourg and comte of Guînes and comte of Benon and baron of Craon and baron of Royan and baron of Sully and 
2 CONC baron of L'Ile-Bouchard and baron of Brandois and baron of Mauléon and baron of Mareuil and baron of Marans and baron of Rochefort and baron of Sainte-Hermine and baron of Doué.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life The la Trémoille family, inheriting the county of Laval after the death of Guy XX of the Laval family, the last representative of that county's direct line. This inheritance obliged the descendents of Anne of Laval, and of Fr
2 CONC ançois de la Trémoille, to come to stay on the banks of the Mayenne occasionally.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 31 October 1537 François lost the châtellenie of Rochefort. In effect, a decree of the parlement de Paris dating to 10 March 1536 reunited Rochefort with his domain. The royal officers, always attentive to conserving the intere
2 CONC sts of their master, were justified by the tenacity of the La Trémoille family, shown especially by a royal debt of 18 000 écus to the family since the battle of Castillon in 1453.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 23 January 1521 he married Anne de Montfort-Laval (1505-1554), daughter of Guy XVI de Laval and of Charlotte d'Aragon-Naples. Their 10 children were :
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis III de la Trémoille who succeeded his father, 
2 CONT
2 CONT François, count of Benon and baron of Montagu († 1555), who married Françoise du Bouchet, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, baron of Mauléon and baron of Marans, abbot of Saint-Laon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Georges, baron of Royan and baron of Olonne and lord (seigneur) of Saujon and of Kergolay († December 1584), who married Madeleine de Luxembourg (daughter of François II vicomte de Martigues) (they were the parents of Gilbert, bar
2 CONC on then from October 1592 marquis of Royan, and baron then from January 1600 count of Olonne, who died 25 July 1603), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Claude, baron of Noirmoutiers and lord of Mornac, of Châteauneuf-sur-Sarthe, of Saint-Germain, of Buron, and of La Roche-Diré († 1566), who married Antoinette de Maillé, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Louise baroness of Rochefort († 1569) who married Philippe de Lévis, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacqueline, baroness of Marans, of Sainte-Hermine, of Brandois, and of La Mothe-Achard († 1599), who married Louis IV de Bueil, comte de Sancerre, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte who became a nun. 
