2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p10595.htm#i105949
2 CONT *Eleanor Sinclair1
2 CONT *F, #105949, d. 21 March 1518/19
2 CONT *Last Edited=25 Apr 2008
2 CONT *     Eleanor Sinclair was the daughter of William Sinclair, 1st Earl of Caithness and Marjory Sutherland.2,3 She married John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl, son of Sir James Stewart of Lorn and Lady Joan Beaufort, before 19 April 1
2 CONC 475.3 She died on 21 March 1518/19.3 She was buried at Dunkeld Cathedral, Dunkeld, Perthshire, Scotland.3
2 CONT *     As a result of her marriage, Eleanor Sinclair was styled as Countess of Atholl before 19 April 1475. From before 19 April 1475, her married name became Stewart.
2 CONT *Children of Eleanor Sinclair and John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl
2 CONT **1.Lady Elizabeth Stewart+
2 CONT **2.John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Atholl+3 b. a 1475, d. 1521
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm JOHN Stewart, son of JAMES Stewart, the Black Knight of Lorn & his wife Joan Beaufort ([1440]-the Laighwood 15 Sep 1512, bur Dunkeld Cathedral).  Earl of Atholl 1457. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([1459/60]) as her third husband, MARGARET Douglas "the Fair Maid of Galloway", widow of WILLIAM Douglas Earl of Douglas and divorced wife (secondly) of JAMES Douglas Earl of Douglas, daughter of ARCHIBALD Douglas Earl o
2 CONC f Douglas & his second wife Eupheme Graham of Strathearn (-[21 Jan 1473/early 1475]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (before 19 Apr 1475) ELEANOR Sinclair, daughter of WILLIAM Sinclair Earl of Caithness & his second wife Marjory Sutherland of Dunbeath (-21 Mar 1518, bur Dunkeld Cathedral). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl John & his first wife had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         JANET (-Strathbogie 27 Oct 1510).  m (contract 14 Oct 1474) as his first wife, ALEXANDER Gordon Master of Huntly, son of GEORGE Gordon Earl of Huntly & his first wife Elizabeth Douglas Dowager Ctss of Moray née Dunbar o
2 CONC f the Earls of Moray (-Perth 21 Jan 1524, bur Perth Dominican Friars).  He succeeded his father in 1501 as Earl of Huntly. 
2 CONT 2.         CATHERINE .  m as his first wife, JOHN Forbes, son of WILLIAM Forbes Lord Forbes & his wife Christian Gordon of the Earls of Huntly (-1547).
2 CONT 3.         three daughters . 
2 CONT 4.         ELIZABETH .  m (before 1483) as his second wife, ANDREW Gray Lord Gray, son of PATRICK Gray Master of Gray & his second wife Annabel Forbes (-Feb 1514).
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl John & his second wife had eleven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         JOHN (-1521).  Earl of Atholl.    -        see below. 
2 CONT 6.         ANDREW (-1542).  Bishop of Caithness 1518.
2 CONT 7.         JEAN .  m as his first wife, ROBERT Gordon of Pitlurgo, son of ---.
2 CONT 8.         ELSPETH .  m ([1510]) ROBERT Innes of Innermarky, son of ---.
2 CONT 9.         MARJORY (-1524).  m COLIN Campbell of Glenurchy, son of --- (-1523).
2 CONT 10.      MARGARET .  m WILLIAM Murray of Tullibardine, son of --- (-killed in battle 1513).
2 CONT 11.      ISABEL .  m as his second wife, ALEXANDER Robertson of Struan, son of ---. 
2 CONT 12.      ELISABETH .  m firstly (contract 19 Jan 1511, Papal dispensation 29 Jan 1511) JOHN Stuart Earl of Lennox, son of MATTHEW Stuart Earl of Lennox & his second wife Elizabeth Hamilton (-murdered [Linlithgow] 4 Sep 1526).  m s
2 CONC econdly (1529) as his second wife, NINIAN Lord Ross, son of --- (-1556).
2 CONT 13.      CHRISTIAN (-1538).  m as his first wife, NEIL Stuart of Garth, son of --- (-1554).
2 CONT 14.      MARGARET [Isabel].  m ROBERT Robertson of Struan, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT #[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 644. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peer
2 CONC age and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT #[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 230. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT #[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct
2 CONC  or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 313. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT #This person and their pedigree are currently documented from "The Royal Lineage of Our Noble and Gentle Families together with Their Paternal Ancestry" Compiled by Joseph Foster, 1885 [Source: http://www.archive.org/details/royal
2 CONC lineageofou02fost ]
2 CONT #"Red Book of Scotland, Volume 9" (Smi-You). Pages 580-582. < [https://www.ancestry.com/search/collections/62525/records/61048?_phcmd=u(%27https://www.ancestry.com/search/collections/62525/?name=john_stewart&birth=1440&death=1512&
2 CONC count=50&successSource=Search&queryId=5a027571-b213-4659-9f08-e627e26176d9%27,%27successSource%27) Ancestry.com] >; ([https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000216556017831&graph_node_id=profile-10029640&mode=tagged Docume
2 CONC nt attached]).  Sir John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl, m. firstly, by 25 March 1460, to Margaret, daughter of Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Douglas, by whom he was the father of: Janet, married Alexander Gordon; Catherine, married
2 CONC  John, 6th Lord Forbes; Elizabeth Stewart, married before 1483, to Andrew, 2nd Lord Gray, (he was widower of Janet, only daughter of Robert, Lord Keith, by whom he had issue. he d. in February of 1514), and had issue. He married s
2 CONC econdly, by 19 April 1475, to Eleanora, daughter of William Sinclair, Earl of Orkney and Caithness (she d. on 21 March 1518) .... and by whom he had further issue [2 sons and 9 daughters].  
2 CONT # https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00006027&tree=LEO cites
