1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET MURRAY===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to George Crawford, writing in his Peerage account of the Stewart earls of Buchan (published in 1716), Margaret Murray was a daughter of Murray of Philliphaugh. Crawford cited: "Mr. Martin of Clermont's  collections i
2 CONC n the hands of his son" as the source of his information, [https://archive.org/details/peerageofscotlan00craw/page/99/mode/1up The Peerage of Scotland: 48] alternatively described by him, as "Mr. Martine of Clearmont's Genealogica
2 CONC l Collections" in his account of the Stewart Earls of Traquair. [https://archive.org/details/peerageofscotlan00craw/page/967/mode/1up Ibidem: 480]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Douglas's account of the Stewart Earls of Buchan, published forty-eight years later (in 1764), follows Crawford's earlier account, saying that Margaret Murray was a daughter of Murray of Philiphaugh, [https://quod.li
2 CONC b.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/1:48?rgn=div1;view=fulltext;q1=traquair The Peerage of Scotland 94] but Douglas went further in his account of the Stewart earls of Traquair, identifying Margaret as a daughter of Patrick Murr
2 CONC ay of Philiphaugh. He did not produced any evidence in support of this new claim, for which he simply cited his earlier account of the Buchan family "for which vide title Stewart earl of Buchan, page 94th". [https://quod.lib.umich
2 CONC .edu/cgi/t/text/pageviewer-idx?cc=ecco;c=ecco;idno=004896980.0001.000;node=004896980.0001.000:242;seq=706;q1=traquair;page=root;view=text Douglas: The Peerage of Scotland 673]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Lands of Traquair===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 18 May 1491 James Stewart, earl of Buchan, gave the barony of Traquair to his bastard son James, and reserved an annualrent from the same to Margaret Murray. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/450/mode/
2 CONC 1up RMS: 2128]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Lands of Berrybus===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 4 March 1492 Margaret Murray and her son James Stewart were granted a three year lease for the lands of Berrybus in the lordship of Etttrick Forest. The lease was granted with the consent of the earl of Buchan. [https://arch
2 CONC ive.org/details/exchequerrollsof10scot/page/736/mode/1up ERS X: 736] The lease was renewed on 30 April 1499,  [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof11scot/page/398/mode/1up ERS XI: 398] and again on 15 April 1501. On this l
2 CONC ast ocassion John Murray of Falahill became pledge for them. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof11scot/page/459/mode/1up ERS XI: 459]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Lands of Ploro===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 4 March 1492 Margaret Murray and her son James Stewart were granted a lease for the lands of Ploro in the lordship of Ettrick Forest. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof10scot/page/738/mode/1up ERS X: 738] The leas
2 CONC e was renewed on 30 April 1499, [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof11scot/page/401/mode/1up ERS: 401] and again on 15 April 1501. On this last occasion John Murray of Falahill became pledge for them. [https://archive.org
2 CONC /details/exchequerrollsof11scot/page/458/mode/1up ERS XI: 458]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Lands of Cassoquhy===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Stewart, earl of Buchan, was granted a three year lease for the lands of Cassoquhy in the lordship of Methven on 3 December 1495. He gave it to Margaret Murray and her son James Stewart .[https://archive.org/details/exche
2 CONC querrollsof10scot/page/745/mode/1up ERS X: 745]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Margaret Murray, here treated. She was alive on 15 April 1501, when the lands of Berrybus and Ploro were set in rental to her and her son James Stewart, [https://archive.org
2 CONC /details/exchequerrollsof11scot/page/459/mode/1up ERS XI: 459] but the annualrent from the lands and barony of Traquair that was granted to her on 18 May 1491 is not mentioned in her grandson's charter for the same dated 11 August
2 CONC  1512, and it seems quite likely, therefore, probable even, that she died before this date. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/817/mode/1up RMS: 3761]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Murray, here treated, is said to have married William Murray. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/267/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 267] The Scots Peerage account of the Stewart Earls of Bucha
2 CONC n does not say who her husband was but it is possible that he was William Murray of Traquair. As much is certainly suggested by the fact that James, earl of Buchan. gave her an annualrent from the lands of Traquair, when he gave t
2 CONC he barony to their son James on 18 May 1491. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/450/mode/1up RMS: 2128]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bastard Bairns===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to John Milne, writing in the Scots Peerage account of the Stewart, Earls of Buchan, James Stewart, earl of Buchan, had: "several natural children by Margaret Murray, widow of William Murray". [https://archive.org/det
2 CONC ails/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/267/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 267]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Stewart-of-Traquair/6000000002188050777?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1597000352066&through=6000000146336598831
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Stewart-Countess-of-Bothwell/6000000012945471288?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1597000370991&through=6000000146336598831
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
