2 CONT '''3 February 1478-79: Charter by which James III, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands and barony of Trakware, together with annualrents from the lands of Quyltheth and Grebistoun, all in the sheriffdom of Peebles,
2 CONC  to his uncle, James, earl of Buchan. These lands were in the king's hands because of the forfeiture of the deceased William of Murray. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/292/mode/1up RMS: 1418]'''
2 CONT
