2 CONT '''18 May 1491: Charter by which James, earl of Buchan, confirms that he has given the lands and barony of Trakware in the sheriffdom of Peebles to his bastard son James Stewart. His gift also included annualrents from the lands o
2 CONC f Quhiltech and Grevistoun, both also in the sheriffdom of Peebles. The barony of Trakware was to be held by James Stewart and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by his brother Alexander Stewart, and his male heirs. James, earl o
2 CONC f Buchan, reserved an annualrent to Margarete Murray, which was to revert to him following her death. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 23 January 1492-93. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi
2 CONC 02scot/page/450/mode/1up RMS: 2128]'''
