2 CONT Margaret, daughter of Patrick Murray, of Falahill & Philiphaugh[1, 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1250.htm#i37534 BIOGRAPHICAL INFORMATION BY OUR ROYAL ANCESTORS]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret married William Murray, son of John Murray and Isobel Hoppar.2. She DID NOT MARRY  Sir James Stewart, 1st Earl of Buchan, Lord Auchterhouse, Sheriff of Angus, Banff, & Forfarshire, High Chamberlain of Scotland, Ambassa
2 CONC dor to France.  He had several illegitimate children by her, including a son (James) & a daughter (Agnes, mistress of King James IV of Scotland, and wife successively of Adam Hepburn, 2nd Earl of Bothwell, of Alexander, 3rd Lord H
2 CONC ome, of Robert, 5th Lord Maxwell, & of Cuthbert Ramsey).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT Identified as "dau of _ Murray of Falahill". Suggested as being of this generation.-Ed..
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT Although he had a wife and children, Hearty James Stewart, Earl of Buchan, inherited  the Beaufort libido.  He had a mistress, Mrs. Margaret Murray, by whom he had two children – James Stewart, 1st Laird of Traquair and Agnes Stew
2 CONC art who continued in the tradition of her mother.  Charles Stuart-Menteth was descended from the son whose descendants were fairly quiet and well behaved, but Ludivina was descended from the wild daughter, Agnes Stewart. 
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIOGRAPHICAL SUMMARY BY WIKIPEDIA'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Stewart,_1st_Earl_of_Buchan#:~:text=%20Family%20%201%20James%20Stewart%2C%201st%20Laird,1511%2C%20secondly%20Alexander%20Home%2C%203rd%20Lord...%20More%20
2 CONT
2 CONT Buchan had several illegitimate children with his mistress Margaret Murray (b. ca. 1446), many of whom were later legitimized by a royal charter issued in 1488–1489.
2 CONT
2 CONT # James Stewart,[5] 1st Laird of Traquair (1480–1513),[citation needed] was the founder of the Traquair family. He was gifted the Traquair estate by his father in 1491. He obtained letters of legitimation, and married the heiress 
2 CONC of the Rutherfords, with whom he received the estates of Rutherford and Wells in Roxburghshire.[5] He was killed at the Battle of Flodden Field.[5] He was the ancestor of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Traquair.
2 CONT # Lady Agnes Stewart, married first Adam Hepburn, 2nd Earl of Bothwell in August 1511, secondly Alexander Home, 3rd Lord Home, thirdly John Maxwell, 4th Lord Maxwell and fourthly Cuthbert Ramsay.[6] They had at least eight childre
2 CONC n. Adam Hepburn, 2nd Earl of Bothwell was killed at the Battle of Flodden Field on 9 September 1513, she died in February, 1557.
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
