1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES STEWART OF TRAQUAIR===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Stewart of Traquair died on 9 September 1513, having been killed in action at the Battle of Flodden in Northumberland, England. [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc359672001 Foundation for Mediev
2 CONC al Genealogy: Stewart Earls of Buchan]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 August 1512: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/817/mode/1up RMS: 3761]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Secondary Source Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. Gen
2 CONC eral Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), 1153 pp. including indexes and Errata]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc359672001 Foundation for Medieval Genealogy: Stewart Earls of Buchan]
2 CONT # [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2501.htm#i25009 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT
2 CONT Buchan had several illegitimate children with his mistress Margaret Murray (b. ca. 1446), many of whom were later legitimized by a royal charter issued in 1488–1489.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stewart,[5] 1st Laird of Traquair (1480–1513),[citation needed] was the founder of the Traquair family. He was gifted the Traquair estate by his father in 1491. He obtained letters of legitimation, and married the heiress of
2 CONC  the Rutherfords, with whom he received the estates of Rutherford and Wells in Roxburghshire.[5] He was killed at the Battle of Flodden Field.[5] He was the ancestor of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Traquair.
2 CONT
2 CONT Attribution
2 CONT  This article incorporates text from a publication now in the public domain: Taylor, James (1889). The great historic families of Scotland 2. London: J.S. Virtue. p. 67.
2 CONT  This article incorporates text from a publication now in the public domain: Mackintosh, John (1898). Historic earls and earldoms of Scotland. W. Jolly. pp. 103, 104. External links Mackintosh, John (2012) [1898]. "Earls of Buchan
2 CONC ". Historic earls and earldoms of Scotland (Electronic ed.). Electric Scotland. SH staff. "The History of Traquair House". Scottish History Online. Retrieved May 2012. Taylor, James (2012) [1887]. "The Stewarts of Traquair". The G
2 CONC reat Historic Families of Scotland (2 volumes) (Electronic ed.). Electric Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
