2 CONT *'''     Lady Eleanor Beauchamp was born between 1407 and 1408 at Wedgenock, Warwickshire, England.2 She was the daughter''' of Richard Beauchamp, 13th Earl of Warwick and Elizabeth de Berkeley.1,3 '''She married, firstly, Thomas 
2 CONC de Ros, 8th Lord de Ros of Helmsley''', son of William de Ros, 6th Lord de Ros of Helmsley and Margaret d'Arundel, '''before 1430.2 She married, secondly, Edmund Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset''', son of John de Beaufort, 1st Earl
2 CONC  of Somerset and Lady Margaret de Holand, '''between 1431 and 1435 in a unlicensed marriage, although this was pardoned on 7 March 1438.2 She married, thirdly, Walter Rokesley.2 She died between 4 March 1466 and 8 March 1468 at Ba
2 CONC ynard's Castle, London, England.2
2 CONT *'''      From before 1430, her married name became de Ros.2 From between 1431 and 1435, her married name became Beaufort.2 Her married name became Rokesley.
