2 CONT *'''Thomas De ROS (9° B. Ros of Hamlake)
2 CONT *Born: 26 Sep 1406
2 CONT *Died: 18 Aug 1430, France
2 CONT *Notes: Brother and heir of John De Ros, 8th Lord Ros, and was aged fourteen at his brother's death. He was knighted BEF the King at Leicester on 19 May 1426, served in France under the Duke of Bedford in 1427, and was summoned to
2 CONC  Parliament in 1429. Died on the 18 Aug 1430, having drowned in the River Seine near Paris, during one of the many small, un-reported actions and skirmishes of the 'Hundred years War' with France.
