2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 April 1535: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland which confirms to William Keith, son and heir of the deceased Robert Keith, Master of Marischal, possession of the barony of Dunotter and other lands, including the lands 
2 CONC of Auchrosk, Auchincloich, Fornocht, Warderis, Leyluge, and others in the Sheriffdom of Aberdeen, which had previously been held in conjuct fee and liferent by the deceased Robert, Master of Marischal, and his wife LADY BEATRICIS 
2 CONC DOWGLAS: "necnon  terras  de Auchrosk,  Auchincloich,  Fornocht,  Warderis,  Leyluge,  Lauehintulich,  Tulybyn, Tortowy,  Auchquhrynnny,  Drumnahaith, Ladach  et  Mylneboy,  vic.  Abirdene que fuerunt  dicti  Rob. et  Beatricis (D
2 CONC owglas) ejus  spouse  in  conjuneta  infeodatione,  et per  mortem  dicti  Rob. et  renunciationem dicte  Beat, regi  devenerunt". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/68/mode/1up RMS: charter number 302]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 May 1527: Instrument of Assignation by Gilbert Keith of Troup, in favour of Isobel Forbes, his spouse, of £100 scots, in bond by LADY BEATRICE DOUGLASSE, relict of Robert, Master of Marischal, and of an annualrent from the l
2 CONC ands of [ - ] stoun, We[dr]yllhill, Killinwardeis, Knoxstrainhaugh, Dwrn, Auchnahamperis, Pratstoun, [?N]eichtfeild and [destroyed], granted to the said LADY BEATRICE DOUGLAS, by letters patent from the day of the death of William
2 CONC , Earl Marischal, until the legal age of 21 of William, Earl Marischal, her grandson. Witnesses William Keith and John Byssat, household servants of the said lord. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.as
2 CONC px?reference=GD57%2f1%2f133A&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrice+douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Records of Messrs Burnett and Reid, Advocates, Aberdeen, reference GD57/1/133A]'''
2 CONT
