2 CONT == PATRICK STEWART OF STICKS ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Stewart of Sticks, here treated, married Elizabeth Butter, daughter of John Butter of Gormack.   [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f147%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=
2 CONC n&k=elizabeth+butter&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD112/2/147/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 January 1553-54: Charter by John, earl of Athole, with consent of Mr George Cuik, canon of Dunkeld, curator 'in hac parte', to Patrick Stewart, son of deceased John Stewart of Stukis, kt., and heirs of said Patrick and Eliza
2 CONC beth Butter, his future spouse, daughter of John Butter of Gormok, of lands of Middill Stukis, Rynnynuik, Borlande, Droume of Stukis, Croft Morane, Garf in Glenquheycht, with mill, 15 January 1553/4. Signed by the earl. Witnesses:
2 CONC  Thomas Stewart of Garntullie, John Reid of Stralocht, John Innis and John Tarlochtsoun. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f147%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+butte
2 CONC r&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/147/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 Apr 1560  [5] GD112/2/147/14 1. Procuratory by David, lord Drummond, appointing William Drummond of Lorntie as procurator to warn Patrick Stewart, brother and heir of deceased James Stewart of Ballachane, and Alexander Stewar
2 CONC t, his natural son, to compeir within parish kirk of Perth on 29 May next 'betwix the sone rising and toganging of that ilk thairupon the burde of the communioune sumtyne quhair the hie alter stude situat and fundat', to receive r
2 CONC edemption money of £100, that is, five score pounds scots, of 40s worth of lands of old extent called Westir Stukis, occupied by deceased sir James McGregor, dean of Lesmoir, with woods, fishing on the water of Tay, pasture and gr
2 CONC azing in Leidchrosk, in lordship of Atholl, sheriffdom of Perth, 4 April 1560. Signed by granter; applied seal. Witnesses: William Drummond of Ballocht, George Drummond, his son and apparent heir, Hercules Lindesay, George Drummon
2 CONC d alias Gawen, Patrick Lindesay and  27 Nov 1564  [5] GD112/2/147/14  8. Signet letters charging Patrick Stewart, brother and heir of deceased John Stewart of Ballachane, and Alexander Stewart, natural son to said John, pretended 
2 CONC heritable possessors of lands called the Stewkis Waster, to compeir 10 January next to come, to answer at instance of David, lord Drummond, 27 November 1564. Endorsed with execution, 5, 7 December 1564, by William Moresoun. Witnes
2 CONC ses: William Drummond of Balloch, James Kinross of Kypanross, James Hering of Drummes, George Drummond of Blair and James Drummond. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f147%2f1
2 CONC 4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD112%2f2%2f147%2f14&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/2/147/14]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
