1 NAME Robert /Hamilton/ Seigneur d'Aubigny
2 GIVN Robert
2 SURN Hamilton
2 NSFX Seigneur d'Aubigny
2 _MARNM Hamilton
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 21 MAR 1476
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1543
1 OCCU Lord of Aubigny
1 TITL Hon.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ROBERT HAMILTON Seigneur d'Aubigny===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Darryl Lundy's Peerage, Hon. Robert Hamilton, Seigneur d'Aubigny, was the son of James Hamilton, 1st Lord Hamilton and Mary Stewart, Princess of Scotland. He died in 1543. He gained the title of Seigneur d'Aubigny.
2 CONC  Lundy's account cites Britain's Royal Families.The Complete Genealogy. By Alison Weir (The Bodley Head, London,1999), p. 234. [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10829.htm Darryl Lundy's Peerage]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Stewart,_Countess_of_Arran#Marriages_and_issue His Father and Mother: Biographical Summary by Wikipedia]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In early 1474, Mary married secondly as his second wife, James Hamilton, 1st Lord Hamilton, who was almost forty years her senior. They received a papal dispensation on 26 April 1476 thus legitimising the two children already b
2 CONC orn to them. Together James and Mary had three children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''James Hamilton, 1st Earl of Arran (1475–1529), married firstly in 1490 Elizabeth Home by whom he had two daughters; he divorced Elizabeth in 1504. He married secondly in 1516, Janet Bethune, daughter of Sir David Bethune, 1st
2 CONC  of Creich and Janet Duddlingston.[5] by whom he had three children including his heir, James Hamilton, Duke of Châtellerault, 2nd Earl of Arran (c.1516- 22 January 1575), heir presumptive to the Kingdom of Scotland (2 July 1536 –
2 CONC  22 May 1540), (April 1541- 8 December 1542), (14 December 1542 – 19 June 1566), (29 July 1567 – 22 January 1575); Regent of Scotland (1542–1554).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Hon. Elizabeth Hamilton (died after April 1531), married 9 April 1494 Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox, by whom she had issue. The Lennox Stewarts, of whom Henry Stuart, Lord Darnley, the second husband of Mary, Queen of S
2 CONC cots was the most notable, derived their claim to the Scottish throne from Elizabeth's son John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Robert Hamilton, Seigneur d'Aubigny (21 March 1476 - 1543).  He was born in Brodick Castle, Hamilton, Torrence, Lanarkshire, Scotland. He died in 1543 in Torrence, Lanarkshire, Scotland, when he was 66 years old. According to
2 CONC  some records, he married (Elizabeth?) Campbell, the daughter of Campbell (Goodman) of Glaister, or Glacester (Angus), the niece of the Sheriff of Ayr [the latter of whom also had connection to the earls of Lennox]. They had at le
2 CONC ast two (claimed) children: Janet Hamilton, born in 1500, who wed Alexander Burnet, 4th Baron & 9th Laird of Leys; and Matthew Hamilton, born in 1512, who wed Jean Muirhead of Torrence.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Stewart,_Countess_of_Arran#Marriages_and_issue Wikipedia: Mary Stewart]
