1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anna van Egmont the Elder, who had married shortly after August 26, 1523, and lived at Ooidonk Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.historici.nl/Onderzoek/Projecten/DVN/lemmata/data/Egmont '''Historici.nl''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLEMISH%20NOBILITY.htm#JosephMontmorencydied1530 v4.3 Updated 28 December 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT JOSEPH de Montmorency (-1530, bur Weert).  Heer van Nevele.  m (contract 26 Aug 1523) as her first husband, '''ANNA van Egmond''', daughter of FLORIS van Egmond Heer van Buren & his wife Margareta van Berg.  She married secondly J
2 CONC an Graaf van Horne.  Joseph & his wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          PHILIPPE de Montmorency (1526-beheaded Brussels 5 Jun 1568, bur Kempen).  Heer van Nevele.  Jan Graaf van Horne (his stepfather) appointed Philippe de Montmorency Heer van Nevele as his heir, the heirship eventually pa
2 CONC ssing to Eberhard Graf von Solms and his wife Sabine van Egmond under the 31 Oct 1598 testament of his widow[911].  Graaf van Horne.  m as her first husband, WALPURGA von Neuenahr, daughter of WILHELM Graf von Neuenahr & his wife 
2 CONC Anna von Werde Gräfin von Mörs und Saarwerden (-Utrecht 23 May 1600).  She married secondly Adolf von Neuenahr Herr von Alpen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         FLORIS de Montmorency (1528-beheaded Oct 1570).  Heer van Nevele.  m (1565) HELENE de Melun, daughter of HUGUES de Melun Prince d’Epinoy & his wife Yolande de Werchin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)        MARIE de Montmorency ).  An epitaph at Lalaing records the burial of “Charles comte de Lalaing...” who married secondly “Marie de Montmorency” from whom he had sons and one daughter[912].  m firstly ([1550]) as his sec
2 CONC ond wife, CHARLES Comte de Lalaing, son of CHARLES Comte de Lalaing & his wife Jacqueline de Luxembourg ([1506]-Brussels 21 Nov 1558, bur Lalaing).  m secondly (1562) as his second wife, PETER ERNST Graf von Mansfeld, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv)       ELEONORE de Montmorency ).  Dame de Montigny.  m firstly PONCE de Lalaing Seigneur de Bugnicourt, son of ---.  m secondly (contract 9 Nov 1560) ANTOINE de Lalaing Graaf van Hoogstraten, son of PHILIPPE de Lalaing Graaf v
2 CONC an Hoogstraten, Baron d’Escornaix & his wife Anne de Rennebourg (Brussels [1535]-Reims 11 Dec 1568). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
