1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jeanne married her first husband in August 1501, shortly after her legitimisation. He was Jean Aubin, Seigneur de Malicorne. The marriage was childless. Sometime after his death, she married secondly, Jean IV de Lo
2 CONC ngwy, Seigneur de Givry, Baron of Pagny and of Mirebeau, by whom she had three daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Francoise de Longwy, Dame de Pagny and de Mirebeau (c.1510- after 14 April 1561), on 10 January 1526, she married firstly, Philippe de Chabot, Seigneur De Brion, Count of Charny and Buzançois, Admiral of France (c.1492- 1 June 154
2 CONC 3), by whom she had six children; in 1545, she married secondly, Jacques de Perusse, Seigneur d'Escars, by whom she had a son, Cardinal Anne d'Escars de Givry, a Benedictine churchman who was also the Bishop of Lisieux and the Bis
2 CONC hop of Metz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claude Louise de Longwy, Abbess of Jouarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacqueline de Longwy, Countess of Bar-sur-Seine (before 1520- 28 August 1561), married in 1538, Louis III de Bourbon, Duke of Montpensier, by whom she had six children, including Charlotte of Bourbon, the third wife of William The
2 CONC  Silent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne's husband died in 1520. His titles were inherited by their eldest daughter, Francoise.
