1 CONT [edit] Marriage and Issue
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles VI married:
1 CONT
1 CONT Isabeau of Bavaria (1371 – September 24, 1435) on July 17, 1385.
1 CONT Name Birth Death Notes
1 CONT Charles, Dauphin September 26, 1386 December 28, 1386 Died young. No issue. First Dauphin.
1 CONT Joan June 14, 1388 1390 Died young. No issue.
1 CONT Isabella November 9, 1389 September 13, 1409 Married (1) Richard II, King of England (1367 - 1400) in 1396. No issue.
1 CONT Married (2) Charles, Duke of Orleans (1394 - 1465) in 1406. Had issue.
1 CONT Joan January 24, 1391 September 27, 1433 Married John VI, Duke of Brittany (1389 - 1442) in 1396. Had issue.
1 CONT Charles of France, Dauphin February 6, 1392 January 13, 1401 Died young. No issue. Second Dauphin.
1 CONT Mary August 24, 1393 August 19, 1438 Never married - became an abbess. No issue. Died of the Plague
1 CONT Michelle January 11, 1395 July 8, 1422 Married Philip the Good, Duke of Burgundy (1396 - 1467) in 1409.
1 CONT Louis, Dauphin January 22, 1397 December 18, 1415 Married Margaret of Burgundy. Third Dauphin.
1 CONT John, Dauphin August 31, 1398 April 4, 1417 Married Jacqueline, Countess of Hainaut (1401 - 1436) in 1415. No issue. Fourth Dauphin.
1 CONT Catherine October 27, 1401 January 3, 1437 Married (1) Henry V, King of England (1387 - 1422) in 1420. Had issue.
1 CONT Married (?) (2) Owen Tudor (1400 - 1461). Had issue.
1 CONT Charles VII, King of France February 22, 1403 July 21, 1461 Married Marie of Anjou (1404 - 1463) in 1422. Had issue. The fifth Dauphin.
1 CONT Philip November 10, 1407 November 10, 1407 Died young. No issue.
1 CONT
1 CONT He also had one illegitimate child by Odette de Champdivers, Marguerite bâtarde de France (1407–1458).
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Cultural References
1 CONT
1 CONT The novel The Notebooks of Malte Laurids Brigge by Rainer Maria Rilke describes the old age of Charles VI at length.
1 CONT
1 CONT The story "Hop-Frog, or The Eight Chained Ourang-Outangs" by Edgar Allan Poe involves a scene strikingly similar to the Bal des Ardents. (Full text at Wikisource)
1 CONT
1 CONT The Edith Pattou novel East mentions Charles of France to be the white bear.
1 CONT
1 CONT King Charles VI, and his madness, are mentioned at length in the historical novel Het Woud der Verwachting/Le Foret de Longue Attente/In a Dark Wood Wandering (1949) by Hella S. Haasse.
1 CONT
