1 CONT of maddness lasting from 3-9 months mixed with 3-5 months of sanity.
0 @N6000000004533169744@ NOTE From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Charles VI the Well-Beloved, later known as the Mad (French: CharlesVI le Bien-Aimé, later known as le Fol) (December 3, 1368 - October21, 1422) was a King of France (1380 - 1422) and a member of theValois Dynasty.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was born in Paris, the son of King Charles V and Jeanne de Bourbon.At the age of eleven, he was crowned King of France in 1380 in thecathedral at Reims. Until he took complete charge as king in 1388,France was run by his uncle,
1 CONC  Philip the Bold.
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles VI was known both as Charles the Mad and as Charles the WellBeloved, since, beginning in his mid twenties, he experienced bouts ofpsychosis. These fits of madness would occur periodically for the restof his life. Doctors t
1 CONC oday believe, based on his ups and downs, thathe may in fact have suffered from bipolar disorder.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1.Isabeau de Bavière (1371-September 24, 1435) on July 17, 1385.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 1. Charles (September 26, 1386 - December 28, 1386)
1 CONT 2. Jeanne (June 14, 1388 - 1390)
1 CONT 3. Isabella of Valois (November 09, 1389 - September 13, 1409),married Richard II of England
1 CONT 4. Jeanne (January 24, 1391 - September 27, 1433), married John VI,Duke of Brittany
1 CONT 5. Charles (February 06, 1392 - January 13, 1401)
1 CONT 6. Marie (August 24, 1393 - August 19, 1438), an abbess
1 CONT 7. Michèle (January 11, 1395 - July 08, 1422)
1 CONT 8. Louis, Duke of Guyenne (January 22, 1396 - December 18, 1415),married Marguerite of Burgundy
1 CONT 9. Jean, Duke of Touraine (August 31, 1398 - April 04, 1417), marriedJacqueline, Countess of Hainaut
1 CONT 10. Catherine (October 27, 1401 - January 03, 1437), married Henry Vof England and Owen Tudor
1 CONT 11. King Charles VII (February 22, 1403 - July 21, 1461)
1 CONT 12. Philippe (November 10, 1407 - November 10, 1407)
1 CONT 2. Odette de Champdivers
1 CONT
1 CONT Child:
1 CONT 1. Marguerite bâtarde de France (1407-1458)
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles VI's reign was marked by the continuing war with the English(the Hundred Years' War), culminating in 1415 when the French army wasdefeated at the Battle of Agincourt. In 1420, Charles signed theTreaty of Troyes which recog
1 CONC nized Henry V of England as his successorand meant his own son could not succeed him (see English Kings ofFrance). Many citizens, including Joan of Arc, believed that the kingonly agreed to such disastrous and unprecedented terms,
1 CONC  under themental stress of his illness and that as a result France could not beheld to them.
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles VI died in 1422 at Paris and is interred with his wife,Isabeau de Bavière in Saint Denis Basilica.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was eventually succeeded by his son Charles VII.
