1 CONC he unquestionably legitimate descendants ofthe second marriage over who should be on the Scottish throne. Matterscame to a head in February, 1437, when James was assassinated by agroup of Scots led by Sir Robert Graham while stayi
1 CONC ng at the FriarsPreachers Monastery in Perth.
