0 @N6000000002188307919@ NOTE Blanca of Bourbon
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche de Bourbon (1339 – 1361) was daughter of Peter I, Duke of Bourbon and Isabella of Valois.
1 CONT
1 CONT On 3 July 1353 she married King Peter of Castile.
1 CONT
1 CONT Eventually she was imprisoned in the castle of Arevalo.
1 CONT
1 CONT She died in Medina Sidonia at the age of twenty-two. The legend says that she was killed by a crossbowman sent by the king himself. Another legend speaks of poisoning.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Hale, Edward Everett, and Susan Hale. The Story of Spain. Story of the nations. New York: G.P. Putnam's Sons, 1886. googlebooks.com Accessed November 16,2007
1 CONT     * Jones, William H. Blanche de Bourbon, and other poems. London: Hookham and Sons, 1855. googlebooks.com Accessed November 16, 2007
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Maria of Portugal Queen Consort of Castile and Leon
1 CONT 1353–1361
1 CONT Succeeded by
1 CONT Juana Manuel of Castile
