0 @N6000000002329575622@ NOTE Originally born John Stewart, King Robert III of Scotland, changed his name to Robert when he ascended the throne. He was named Earl of Carrick 22Jun1368. Although he reigned as King of Scotland from 1390-1406, history and folklor
1 CONC e tell us that 
1 CONT he was too sick to rule due to a kick from a horse.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was born in 1337, and legitimated (dispensation) in 1347. In c1367 he married Annabella Drummond (c1349-1401). They had eight children:
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Margaret Stewart (m. by 1390, Archibald Douglas, 4th Earl of Douglas, [d. 17Aug1424])
1 CONT
1 CONT    2. Elizabeth Stewart (by 1378-by 1439; m. aft 03Nov1411, Sir James Douglas [d. by May 1441])
1 CONT
1 CONT    3. David Stuart of Rothesay (b. 24Oct1378, Duke of Rothesay)
1 CONT
1 CONT    4. Robert Stewart
1 CONT
1 CONT    5. Lady Mary Stewart
1 CONT
1 CONT    6. Egidia Stewart
1 CONT
1 CONT    7. James I, King of Scotland (Dec1394-21Feb1436/7; m. Joan Beaufort; 3 children)
1 CONT
1 CONT    8. John Stewart of Blackhall and Ardgowan
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT King Robert III of Scotland died 04Apr1406 in Roshsay Castle. He is buried at Paisley Abbey, Renfrewshire, Scotland.
