0 @N6000000004270567748@ NOTE http://www.landersgen.com/landers/62/7284.htm
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Born: 1337, Scotland, England 631,766
1 CONT     * Marriage: Annabella Drummond in 1367 766
1 CONT     * Died: 4 Apr 1406, Rothesay Castle, Isle of Bute, Argyllshire, Scotland at age 69 766
1 CONT     * Buried: 1406, Paisley Abbey, Renfrewshire, Scotland 766
1 CONT
1 CONT    Another name for Robert was John Stewart.
1 CONT
1 CONT   General Notes:
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert III (c. 1340-1406), king of Scotland from 1390 to 1406, son of Robert II. The principal events in Robert's reign were the invasion of Scotland in 1400 by Henry IV of England, who penetrated as far as Edinburgh, and the reta
1 CONC liatory expedition of the Scotch, two years after, under Archibald Douglas, which resulted in the terrible disaster at Homildon Hill. [The Home University Encyclopedia, 1946]
1 CONT
1 CONT John Stewart. Created Earl of Carrick in 1368. Succeeded to the throne as Robert III.{Burke's Peerage} [GADD.GED]
1 CONT
1 CONT   Noted events in his life were:
1 CONT
1 CONT  Title: Earl of Carrick, 1368.
1 CONT
1 CONT  Title: King of Scotland, 1390-1406.
1 CONT
1 CONT  Alt. Death, 4 Apr 1406, Dundonald Castle, Ayrshire, Scotland. 631
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert married Annabella Drummond, daughter of Sir John Drummond and Unknown, in 1367.766 (Annabella Drummond was born about 1350,766 died in Oct 1401 in Scone Palace, Perthshire, Scotland 766,788 and was buried in 1401 in Dunferm
1 CONC line, Fife, Scotland 766.)
0 @N6000000000437356358@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Princess Still Living.
0 @N6000000001783571700@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Lady Mary Stewart was the daughter of Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland and Annabel Drummond.  Lady Mary Stewart gained the title of Princess Mary of Scotland.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriages and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT She married by contract, firstly, George Douglas, 1st Earl of Angus, son of William Douglas, 1st Earl of Douglas and Margaret Stewart, Countess of Angus, on 24 May 1397. As a result of her marriage, Lady Mary Stewart was styled as
1 CONC  Countess of Angus after 24 May 1397. From after 24 May 1397, her married name became Douglas.  They had two children:
1 CONT Lady Elizabeth Douglas
1 CONT William Douglas, 2nd Earl of Angus b. c 1398, d. Oct 1437
1 CONT
1 CONT She married, secondly, Sir James Kennedy of Dunure, younger, son of Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, circa 1404. From circa 1404, her married name became Kennedy.
1 CONT They had the following children:
1 CONT Sir John Kennedy d. a 1434
1 CONT Mary Kennedy
1 CONT Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, 1st Lord Kennedy b. c 1406, d. a 6 Mar 1478/79
1 CONT James Kennedy b. 1405/6, d. Jul 1465
1 CONT
1 CONT She and Sir William Cunningham were engaged in July 1409
1 CONT
1 CONT She married, thirdly, Sir William Graham on 13 November 1413. From 13 November 1413, her married name became Graham.
1 CONT
1 CONT She married, fourthly, Sir William Edmondstone of Culloden in 1425. From 1425, her married name became Edmonstone.  They had one child:
1 CONT Robert Graham
1 CONT
1 CONT Death
1 CONT
1 CONT She died circa 1458. She was buried at Strathbane Church, Scotland
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://thepeerage.com/p10533.htm#i105322>
0 @N6000000004270567679@ NOTE http://www.landersgen.com/landers/62/8174.htm
1 CONT
1 CONT Mary Stewart
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Born: Abt 1380, Dunfermline, Fife, Scotland 631
1 CONT     * Marriage (1): Earl George Douglas, Duke of Angus on 24 Mar 1397 631,766,816
1 CONT     * Marriage (2): Sir James Kennedy, Earl of Dunure in 1405
1 CONT     * Marriage (3): Sir William Cunningham in Jul 1409 766
1 CONT     * Marriage (4): William Graham, Lord of Kincardine on 13 Nov 1413 766
1 CONT     * Marriage (5): William Edmonstone, of Duntreath in 1425 766
1 CONT     * Died: 1458, Scotland, England about age 78 631,766
1 CONT     * Buried: Strathblane Church, Stirling, Scotland
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Mary married Earl George Douglas, Duke of Angus, son of William Douglas and Margaret Stewart, on 24 Mar 1397 631,766.,816 (Earl George Douglas, Duke of Angus was born about 1376 in Mar, Aberdeenshire, Scotland 631 and died in 1402
1 CONC  in Battle of Hameldon Hill, Lancashire, England 631.)
1 CONT
1 CONT Mary next married Sir James Kennedy, Earl of Dunure, son of Sir Gilbert Kennedy and Agnes Maxwell, in 1405. (Sir James Kennedy, Earl of Dunure died on 8 Nov 1408 766.)
1 CONT
1 CONT Mary next married Sir William Cunningham in Jul 1409.766
1 CONT
1 CONT Mary next married William Graham, Lord of Kincardine on 13 Nov 1413.766
1 CONT
1 CONT Mary next married William Edmonstone, of Duntreath in 1425.766 
0 @N6000000002187794458@ NOTE Lady Mary Stewart1,2 (F)
1 CONT b. before 1382, d. circa 1458, #105322
1 CONT Pedigree
1 CONT
1 CONT Father Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland2 b. 1337, d. 4 April 1406
1 CONT Mother Annabel Drummond2 b. circa 1350, d. circa October 1401
1 CONT
1 CONT Last Edited 12 Feb 2006
1 CONT Consanguinity Index 0.0%
1 CONT
1 CONT      Lady Mary Stewart was born before 1382. She was the daughter of Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland and Annabel Drummond.2 She married by contract, firstly, George Douglas, 1st Earl of Angus, son of William Douglas, 1st Earl
1 CONC  of Douglas and Margaret Stewart, Countess of Angus, on 24 May 1397.1 She married, secondly, Sir James Kennedy of Dunure, younger, son of Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, circa 1404.1 She and Sir William Cunningham were engaged in J
1 CONC uly 1409.1 She married, thirdly, Sir William Graham on 13 November 1413.1 She married, fourthly, Sir William Edmondstone of Culloden in 1425.3 She died circa 1458.3 She was buried in Strathbane Church, Scotland.3
1 CONT      Lady Mary Stewart gained the title of Princess Mary of Scotland.4 As a result of her marriage, Lady Mary Stewart was styled as Countess of Angus after 24 May 1397. From after 24 May 1397, her married name became Douglas. From
1 CONC  circa 1404, her married name became Kennedy. From 13 November 1413, her married name became Graham. From 1425, her married name became Edmonstone.
1 CONT
1 CONT Family 1 George Douglas, 1st Earl of Angus b. before 1378, d. after September 1402
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. William Douglas, 2nd Earl of Angus+ b. c 1398, d. Oct 14371
1 CONT    2. Lady Elizabeth Douglas+ b. b 14021
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Family 2 Sir James Kennedy of Dunure, younger b. before 1390, d. before 8 November 1408
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Mary Kennedy+ 5
1 CONT    2. Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, 1st Lord Kennedy+ b. c 1406, d. a 6 Mar 1478/791
1 CONT    3. James Kennedy b. 1405/6, d. Jul 14651
1 CONT    4. Sir John Kennedy b. b 1408, d. a 14341
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Family 3 Sir William Cunningham b. before 1400, d. between 7 August 1413 and December 1414
1 CONT
1 CONT Family 4 Sir William Graham b. before 1374, d. 1424
1 CONT
1 CONT Family 5 Alexander Graham b. before 1398, d. after 10 August 1423
1 CONT Child 
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Robert Graham b. b 14231
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Family 6 Sir William Edmondstone of Culloden b. before 1410, d. circa 1462
1 CONT
1 CONT Citations 
1 CONT
