0 @N6000000002322320679@ NOTE As king, he established Polish suzerainty over Ducal Prussia (East Prussia)
1 CONT and incorporated the duchy of Mazovia into the Polish state. Although he
1 CONT established fiscal and monetary reforms, he often clashed with the Polish
1 CONT Diet over extensions of royal power. In 1521, Sigismund's army, led by one of
1 CONT the principal advisors and commanders, Jan Tarnowski, subdued the Order of
1 CONT the Teutonic Knights, a paramilitary religious order that ruled East Prussia.
