0 @N6000000003658772923@ NOTE From Plantagenet Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT GUY III DE CHÂTILLON, Count of Saint-Pol-sur-Ternoise (Pas-de-Calais), seigneur of Ancre, Lucheux, and Doullens, Grand Butler of France, 2nd son of Guy II de Châtillon, Count of Saint-Pol .... They had two sons ... and five daught
1 CONC ers ....  In 1292 his older brother, Hugh, Count of Blois, surrendered St.-Pol to him.  In 1297 Philippe le Bel, King of France, granted him certain land appurtenant to the monestary of Saint-Lucien de Beauvais.  She joined the En
1 CONC glish court in Gascony in the winter of 1286-87, and subsequently travelled to England with the king and queen in August 1289.  She visited her grandmother, Eleanor of Provence, at Amesbury in Feb. and April 1290.
