0 @N6000000005598760395@ NOTE 1395-1458.  Son of Ferdinand I of Aragon; king of Aragon andSicly(1416-58) and Naples (1443-58).  Queen Joanna II of Naplesadopted Alfonsoas her heir after he defeated her rival LouisIII of Naples in 1421.  Theyquarreled, and afte
1 CONC r her death in1435 Alfonso had to contest the thronewith a rival claimant,Rene of Anjou.  In 1442 he defeated Rene andremained for therest of his life in Naples.  A leading figure of theearlyRenaissance, he favoured men of letters
1 CONC , and his devotion totheclassics was such that a reading from Quintus Curtius is said tohavecured him of a severe illness.
