1 CONT His reign was divided into 2 halves.  During the first the king was harassed by rebellions; during the second by constant ill health and the ambitions of his heir.  These 2 divisions can be studied in dramatic form in the two part
1 CONC s of William Shakespeare's King Henry the Fourth.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry's reign was punctuated by repeated rebellions in the North and the Glyndwr rebellion in the West. Despite this he successfully held the Crown and passed it on to his son, Henry V, though their relationship was always uneasy.
1 CONC  his reign effectively ended all military use of castles in Brecknock.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry IV was born at Bolingbroke in 1367 to John of Gaunt and Blanche of Lancaster. He married Mary Bohun in 1380, who bore him seven children before her death in 1394. In 1402, Henry remarried, taking as his bride Joan of Navarre
1 CONC .
1 CONT Henry had an on-again, off-again relationship with his cousin, Richard II . He was one of the Lords Appellant who, in 1388, persecuted many of Richard's advisor-favorites, but his excellence as a soldier gained the king's favor - 
1 CONC Henry was created Duke of Hereford in 1397. In 1398, however, the increasingly suspicious Richard banished him fov ten years. John of Gaunt's death in 1399 prompted Richard to confiscate the vast Lancastrian estates; Henry invaded
1 CONC  England while Richard was on campaign in Ireland, usurping the throne from the king.
1 CONT
1 CONT The very nature of Henry's usurpation dictated the circumstances of his reign - incessant rebellion became the order of the day. Richard's supporters immediately revolted upon his deposition in 1400. In Wales , Owen Glendower led 
1 CONC a national uprising that lasted until 1408; the Scots waged continual warfare throughout the reign; the powerful families of Percy and Mortimer (the latter possessing a stronger claim to the throne than Henry) revolted from 1403 t
1 CONC o 1408; and Richard Scrope, Archbishop of York, proclaimed his opposition to the Lancastrian claim in 1405.
