1 CONT Biography. Oxford, England: Oxford University Press. </span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 2. ^ Mortimer, Fears of Henry IV, pp. 211-7</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 3. ^ The Book of the Princes of Wales, Heirs to the Crown of England, Dr. John 
1 CONT Doran, London, Richard Bentley, New Burlington Street, Publisher in Ordinary to Her 
1 CONT Majesty, 1860</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 4. ^ Peter McNiven, &quot;The Problem of Henry IV's Health, 1405&#150;1413&quot;, English 
1 CONT Historical Review, 100 (1985), pp. 747&#150;772)</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 5. ^ Debbi Codling, &quot;Henry IV and Personal Piety&quot;, History Today, 57:1 (January 
1 CONT 2007), pp. 23-29.</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 6. ^ ANTIQUARY s9-IX (228): 369. (1902).</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 7. ^ Marks of Cadency in the British Royal Family</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">&#160;&#160; 8. ^ Given-Wilson, Chris (2004). in Alfonso Ant&#243;n, Isabel: Building Legitimacy: 
1 CONT Political Discourses and Forms of Legitimacy in Medieval Societies. Boston, MA: 
1 CONT Brill, p 90. ISBN 9004133054. </span></div>
