0 @N6000000002187845440@ NOTE Louis I of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis I (1304 – August 26, 1346, ruled 1322–1346) was Count of Flanders, Nevers and Rethel. He was the son of Louis, Count of Nevers and Jeanne of Rethel, and grandson of Robert III of Flanders.
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis married Marguerite of France, second daughter of Philip V of France and Jeanne II, Countess of Burgundy. Louis I relied on the aid of his father-in-law to put down the rebellion of Nikolaas Zannekin. Louis was killed in the 
1 CONC Battle of Crécy.
1 CONT
1 CONT He and Marguerite had one son:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Louis II of Flanders (1330–1384), who succeeded him
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
