1 CONT
1 CONT James also loved ships and saw the importance in Scotland having alarge navy. He acquired thirty-eight ships for the Royal Scottish Navyand founded two new dockyards. His finest creation was the carrackGreat Michael. Launched in 1
1 CONC 511 she weighed 1,000 tons, was 240 feetin length and was then the largest ship in Europe.
1 CONT
1 CONT For a time he supported the pretender to the English throne PerkinWarbeck and carried out a brief invasion of England on his behalf.Having fought off the aggression of King Henry VII of England, Jamesrecognized that peace between 
